pped, so the joined sequence takes the width of the leading character (2 cells for a wide emoji), not one cell.\"},{\"n\":10,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/table.py:203\"],\"reason\":\"Table.__init__ declares show_edge: bool = True.\"},{\"n\":11,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/style.py:108-109\"],\"reason\":\"STYLE_ATTRIBUTES contains the key \\\"bold\\\" mapped to \\\"bold\\\".\"},{\"n\":12,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/console.py:2074-2094\",\"rich/console.py:2121-2127\"],\"reason\":\"_write_buffer checks self.legacy_windows (plus fileno) to decide between legacy_windows_render via LegacyWindowsTerm and plain self.file.write of the rendered text.\"},{\"n\":13,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/table.py:670-674\"],\"reason\":\"The code is exactly header_style = get_style(self.header_style or \\\"\\\") + get_style(column.header_style).\"},{\"n\":14,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/style.py:510-511\"],\"reason\":\"Style.parse returns cls.null() when the definition strips to \\\"none\\\" or is empty.\"},{\"n\":15,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/table.py:459-467\"],\"reason\":\"add_row checks is_renderable for each cell and raises errors.NotRenderableError immediately when adding the row.\"},{\"n\":16,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/console.py:2050-2052\"],\"reason\":\"_check_buffer does `del self._buffer[:]` and returns when self.quiet is True.\"},{\"n\":17,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/style.py:340-342\"],\"reason\":\"__bool__ returns `not self._null`, i.e. False for a null style.\"},{\"n\":18,\"label\":\"contradicted\",\"lines\":[\"rich/text.py:1233-1240\"],\"reason\":\"wrap calls divide_line(str(line), width, fold=wrap_overflow == \\\"fold\\\") and only in the non-no_wrap branch, so fold is not always True.\"},{\"n\":19,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"rich/table.py:440-441\"],\"reason\":\"The add_cell closure does column._cells.append(renderable).\"},{\"n\":20,\"label\":\"unverifi